**Verdict:** trust `strained` · value `high` · delight `clear_hit` · recommendation **revise** · **3 blockers, 8 concerns**

**Strongest hit (FAN-H1)** — the constraints passage: *"Everything people read as serenity started as a workaround… She assembled a visual language out of constraints, and the internet read the constraints as a manifesto."* Three things every viewer knows (whisper, bob, dress), each with a boring separate cause, unified into one idea. That's the fan delight test cleared outright. The oatmeal close runs a near-second — it makes her solitude retroactive and involuntary rather than a flex.

**Highest-priority finding (FAN-R1, blocker)** — the draft says in three places that she rebutted the tradwife label only once, in July 2026, after it started costing her money. She rebutted it on the record on **On Purpose with Jay Shetty, 10 July 2025** — 384 days earlier, with the same three arguments including the dishes line the draft treats as a Cooper revelation ("They use me as this poster child of this like very traditional wife and I'm not" / "I work… I travel almost every week" / Lucky does "the dishes or get the kids dressed"). Also GQ, August 2024. This isn't just a date slip — it cascades three ways: it makes the piece **concede more to Levings than the facts require**, it **falsifies the stated evidence for the 8w9 wing call** (which rests entirely on "she did it once… an 8w7 would have gone back at critics repeatedly" — she has), and it misses a second, more direct leg for the anti-retcon spine the draft works hard to build from the lupus post.

Two other blockers, both from one fan-held fact — Whimsy was born 8 April 2024, eclipse day: the cold open calls her "a two-year-old" across a window that began when she was 19 months, and "rang the bell… right after her birthday" contradicts the article's own eight-month timeline and the 17 July remission post.

The one non-obvious concern worth your attention: the section titled **"Why the label stuck in the first place" never names why it stuck**. Her videos open with a request from her husband or a child, then she fills it from scratch in couture — that's the tradwife tableau, in her own edit, a thousand times. The draft quotes @Katwiia asking exactly this question and answers with Utah and Ballerina Farm. Fixing it also strengthens the R1 repair, since the format is the part of the ledger charge that genuinely survives.
